            <ArticleTitle>[Recent new information on epidemiology of headache].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>184-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We reviewed the epidemiology of headache disorders for the most frequent primary headache-syndromes: migraine, tension-type headache and trigemino-autonomic headache syndromes. In the last years scientific data about headache disorders have increased. New studies investigated not only the prevalence of headaches, but also economic costs of this disorder. Epidemiologic headache research also investigates the quality of life.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
